{#- EXPLAIN rather than SELECT: the only question is whether the predicate
    resolves against the candidate's columns, and answering it must not scan
    the table this package exists to sit in front of.

    Worth its own probe because extra_where is raw SQL spliced into the view's
    text. Against a candidate that renamed the column it names, the failure is
    a CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW that raises in the middle of the cutover
    transaction -- correct, since the transaction rolls back, but a much worse
    place to find out than the preflight. -#}
EXPLAIN SELECT 1
FROM {{ source.schema | qi }}.{{ source.table | qi }}
WHERE {{ source.extra_where }}
